  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% limit and 55°C test but drops any sales bar for models above it, allowing the 24-month remediation window to run with no interim cap; per-model results go to buyers and regulators but not to the public. S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 on a rolling 12-month, regulator-validated basis, which is a real exposure for Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) and is not triggered by Hearth 10 (6.4). S3 gives a six-year retrofit window with an alternative-plan escape, and S4 sets built-in suppression at 36 months."
 },
